{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Rg81UcaXYn2n78wwvzJFu2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task. I need to create three test files for the `pkg/format` package:\n\n1. `pkg/format/humansize_test.go` - Tests for HumanSize\n2. `pkg/format/color_test.go` - Tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n3. `pkg/format/pad_test.go` - Tests for PadRight, PadLeft, Columns\n\nLet me review the source code provided in the prompt to understand what I'm testing:\n\n\n- HumanSize converts bytes to human-readable format with binary (1024-based) or SI (1000-based) modes, handling edge cases like zero bytes and formatting decimals based on value magnitude\n- FileTypeColor returns ANSI color codes based on file mode, and Reset returns the reset code\n- ColorEnabled checks if colors should be used (respecting overrides or terminal detection), SetColorEnabled forces the setting, and ResetColorEnabled clears any override\n- PadRight and PadLeft add trailing or leading spaces respectively, while Columns arranges entries into a grid layout based on terminal width\n\nNow I'm writing the test cases for HumanSize, covering binary mode conversions like 512 bytes staying as \"512\", 1024 becoming \"1.0K\", and SI mode with 1000-based conversions like 1000 bytes becoming \"1.0kB\".\n\nI'm tracing through the formatValue logic to understand how it handles the conversion: when there's no suffix it returns the raw integer, when the value is under 10 it formats with one decimal place, otherwise it rounds to the nearest integer and appends the suffix. Now I'm checking the color output for different file types—directories get blue, symlinks cyan, executables green, and special files like pipes and sockets get their own ANSI codes, while the color system can be toggled on or off. I'm also verifying the padding functions work correctly.\n\nI need to be careful with the color tests since SetColorEnabled and ResetColorEnabled modify global state protected by a mutex, so I can't run those tests in parallel or they'll interfere with each other. Let me write out all three test files now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152111,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":152111},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30f6ce8b-19e5-4f5d-a66c-eb0ad304e850","uuid":"dcdc18e7-26e9-4286-8b2d-c2b9526b1227"}
