{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is a stitch task (#5123) from the cobbler orchestrator to create formatting tests for `pkg/format` (srd003-format). Specifically, three test files must be created:\n   - `pkg/format/humansize_test.go` — Tests for HumanSize with binary and SI modes\n   - `pkg/format/color_test.go` — Tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n   - `pkg/format/pad_test.go` — Tests for PadRight, PadLeft, Columns\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: `go test ./pkg/format/... -count=1` must pass, with tests covering HumanSize boundary values (AC2), FileTypeColor for all file types (AC3), and PadRight/PadLeft/Columns edge cases (AC4).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Table-driven Go tests with `t.Run` and named struct rows\n   - `t.Parallel()` required for safe tests, but NOT for tests modifying global state (color override)\n   - `t.Helper()` required on all test helpers\n   - Copyright header required on every Go file\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines (hard limit)\n   - Differential testing pattern (not applicable here — these are unit tests for pkg/)\n   - ANSI escape sequence testing\n   - Unicode rune-based width computation\n   - Column layout algorithm (top-to-bottom, left-to-right fill)\n   - No git commands allowed — orchestrator manages git\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `pkg/format/humansize.go` (existing, provided inline):\n     - Contains `HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string` and `HumanSizeOpts{Binary bool}`\n     - Binary mode: base 1024, suffixes `[\"\", \"K\", \"M\", \"G\", \"T\", \"P\", \"E\"]`\n     - SI mode: base 1000, suffixes `[\"\", \"kB\", \"MB\", \"GB\", \"TB\"]`\n     - `formatValue`: no suffix → `%d`, rounded<10 → `%.1f%s`